H713 Linux: licences and source code
====================================

This system was built by release/build-all.sh of H713 Linux,
https://github.com/well0nez/allwinner-h713-linux. It is free software,
made of many parts under several licences. This file says which parts
are in the image, under which licence each one comes, where its licence
text is, and where its source code is. SOURCES, next to this file,
names the revisions this image was built from.

The texts of the common licences (GPL-2, GPL-3, LGPL-2.1, Apache-2.0,
MPL-2.0 and others) are in /usr/share/common-licenses/.


Parts of the image and their licences
-------------------------------------

On the eMMC ahead of the partitions (the boot chain):

  U-Boot, SPL and U-Boot proper    GPL-2.0-or-later. Source: SOURCES.
  Trusted Firmware-A, BL31         BSD-3-Clause; some files of it under
                                   other permissive licences. The licence
                                   is tf-a/license.rst; tf-a/COPYRIGHTS
                                   lists the copyright lines of every
                                   source file built into BL31, and the
                                   head of each file under another
                                   licence. licenses/BSD-2-Clause is the
                                   text libfdt is used under.
  crust (the firmware of the       BSD-3-Clause or GPL-2.0-only, at your
  ARISC core; boards that name     choice, with a few BSD-1-Clause and
  one only)                        MIT headers: crust/LICENSE.md;
                                   crust/COPYRIGHTS as for BL31.

On the boot partition and in /lib/modules (the kernel):

  Linux with this project's        GPL-2.0, with the syscall note of
  patches, its modules and the     Linux: linux/COPYING. The device
  device trees                     trees are for the most part
                                   GPL-2.0-or-later OR MIT.
  aic8800 Wi-Fi and Bluetooth      GPL-2.0 (modinfo aic8800_fdrv).
  driver (/lib/modules/*/extra)

In the root file system:

  Debian packages                  each under its own licence, stated in
                                   /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.
                                   DEBIAN-SOURCES lists every source
                                   package and its version.
  Mesa (/usr/local)                mostly MIT; licence texts and the note
                                   on its source: /usr/local/share/doc/mesa/
  libva-v4l2-request (images with  GPL-3.0-or-later. Its licence, its
  the media or desktop profile,    source, the patches and the build
  /usr/local/lib/dri)              script: /usr/local/share/doc/libva-v4l2-request/
  This project's programs and      GPL-2.0 (h713-tv, h713-osd, h713-warp,
  scripts (/usr/local, /etc/h713,  h713-power and the others). Source:
  the units in /etc/systemd)       the repository named in SOURCES.
  FreeType, libpng, bzip2, brotli  linked statically into h713-osd and
  and zlib                         h713-settings. FreeType is used under
                                   GPL-2.0, its other choice besides the
                                   FreeType License. The copyright files
                                   of the Debian packages the static
                                   libraries come from are
                                   static/<package>/copyright.

Five packages of the root file system (libgbm1, libegl-mesa0,
libgl1-mesa-dri, mesa-libgallium, libglx-mesa0) are empty stand-ins this
project builds (rootfs/equivs/ in the repository), so that Debian's
packages install against the Mesa in /usr/local. They contain no files.

Not part of this image: the firmware the installer copies from the
owner's own device (the display processor's, the Wi-Fi chip's and the
like) and the device's own keys. They stay what they were, under the
terms the device came with, and this file does not cover them.


Source code
-----------

The source code of this project's own parts, of its patches to Linux,
U-Boot, Trusted Firmware-A, crust, the aic8800 driver and
libva-v4l2-request, and of the scripts that build this image, is in the
repository at the commit SOURCES names. SOURCES also names, for each
upstream, the revision the patches apply to. Debian's source packages
are on deb.debian.org and, by version, on snapshot.debian.org.

The complete corresponding source of this image is the repository with
its submodules at the commit SOURCES names: it is archived next to the
image where it is published (allwinner-h713-linux-<version>-with-
submodules.tar) and reachable as the tag of the same name, which points
at that commit. Linux (kernel.org), the aic8800 driver, crust and
libva-v4l2-request are not copied into it: the repository carries this
project's patches to them, the configurations and the pinned upstream
revisions, and SOURCES names each one. Whoever passes the image on
passes that archive, or the way to it, on with it. Debian's source
packages are on deb.debian.org and, by version, on snapshot.debian.org
(DEBIAN-SOURCES).
